#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008c6610-3637-585c-b3f6-1b02b7f4bd54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3w+4 \\\\ w-5 \\\\ -2w+4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716823} {:answer/id #uuid "0b8c9caa-7348-503c-97f6-4424a954d082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3w-4 \\\\ w-1 \\\\ -2w-2 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716825} {:answer/id #uuid "54cd8138-e7b7-53ea-bffd-f060f5cb12f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3w-4 \\\\ w+3 \\\\ -2w+5 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716832} {:answer/id #uuid "8eeb21d9-d4b9-5dff-990a-47e77975d212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3w-2 \\\\ w-5 \\\\ -2w-5 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716838} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a4b93c-fb36-5634-85f7-580169cc0342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3w-2 \\\\ w+3 \\\\ -2w-4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716856}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716856} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc9a14e-8560-5626-b406-e1fe686ce084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "eb1fd149-6b20-56dc-88e3-b40d77341f44" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y-4z-16w &=18 \\\\ -x+2y-4z-7w &=24 \\\\ -2x-3y+8z+25w &=-37.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -4 & -16 & 18 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 & -7 & 24 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 8 & 25 & -37\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -4 & -16 & 18 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 & -7 & 24 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 8 & 25 & -37\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -8 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 & -7 & 24 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 8 & 25 & -37\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & -15 & 33 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 8 & 25 & -37\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & -15 & 33 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 9 & -19\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 9 & -19\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3w &=-2 \\\\ y-w &=3 \\\\ z+2w &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3w-2 \\\\ y &=w+3 \\\\ z &=-2w-4 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3w-2 \\\\ w+3 \\\\ -2w-4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ec5e4d-c967-56af-b629-e078bde56c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}w+4 \\\\ 3w+5 \\\\ 2w-2 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716858} {:answer/id #uuid "5964d75f-37b6-5f4c-91d9-37445f7bdf45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}w-1 \\\\ 3w+5 \\\\ 2w-5 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716861} {:answer/id #uuid "63de81ce-47a4-51ac-94a1-ca4b6149b51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}w-4 \\\\ 3w+2 \\\\ 2w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716865} {:answer/id #uuid "d137c63d-fdb0-5a67-b5cc-c18ff22cb5c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}w-4 \\\\ 3w-5 \\\\ 2w-6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716880} {:answer/id #uuid "f62dc61f-0c6c-520f-8fab-65275cbab1c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}w+4 \\\\ 3w+2 \\\\ 2w-1 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716885}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716865} :answer-field/id #uuid "e149d5aa-9788-5e0b-980d-8f02dbf6171c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "36c899b0-8021-549b-952d-610c85435ffb" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y-2z+8w &=-6 \\\\ -x+4y-2z-7w &=18 \\\\ -x+3y+z-10w &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -2 & -7 & 18 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & -10 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -2 & -7 & 18 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & -10 & 7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -2 & -7 & 18 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & -10 & 7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 & 15 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & -10 & 7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -6 & 4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -6 & 4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4 & -6\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-w &=-4 \\\\ y-3w &=2 \\\\ z-2w &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=w-4 \\\\ y &=3w+2 \\\\ z &=2w-3 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}w-4 \\\\ 3w+2 \\\\ 2w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f0dfb54-0057-573e-8c42-e71a3d63b4cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3w-3 \\\\ -w-6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716863} {:answer/id #uuid "896e71c3-78ba-506b-ae3c-ebc4821145cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -3w+3 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716870} {:answer/id #uuid "97fb0996-40d4-5bb0-8c28-186b839493a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3w-3 \\\\ -w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716871} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e8e0e3-fc24-5c4b-9b1d-06fc62cd4e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -3w-2 \\\\ -w+4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716876} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9178ad-0b95-5d16-9a39-046afac1fa1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3w-2 \\\\ -w+1 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716884}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716884} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5f2013-0fb9-55f8-a8c2-33f52d10df18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6edf95c4-59e5-5172-a79d-8c45ae85d520" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y-2z+4w &=2 \\\\ 2x+5y-8z+7w &=-10 \\\\ 2x+y+2z+5w &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -8 & 7 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 5 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -8 & 7 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 5 & 8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -8 & 7 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 5 & 8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 5 & 8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4 \\\\ y+3w &=-2 \\\\ z+w &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4 \\\\ y &=-3w-2 \\\\ z &=-w+1 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3w-2 \\\\ -w+1 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82bc85e3-4325-53e3-ab72-36adfc175db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2w+4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716869} {:answer/id #uuid "c00a7270-f6c1-57da-9280-e0af7a851b0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2w-6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716878} {:answer/id #uuid "cef253ba-f03d-5b57-862a-5039971203b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2w-1 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716879} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e9dd88-abac-542a-891c-aa0bbc4d2371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716881} {:answer/id #uuid "de1cc7f3-7101-5ef9-a3aa-e3076b5b98d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2w+3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716869} :answer-field/id #uuid "99efc5a7-7db7-52dc-9b3a-db545cc21b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6fadffc5-bcbe-57df-9077-f60f6c193d29" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y+2z-2w &=2 \\\\ -x+4y+2z-5w &=26 \\\\ x+y+5z-9w &=27.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 2 & -5 & 26 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -9 & 27\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & 2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 2 & -5 & 26 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -9 & 27\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 2 & -5 & 26 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -9 & 27\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -6 & 27 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -9 & 27\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -6 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -8 & 26\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & -8 & 26\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4 & 8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+w &=2 \\\\ y &=5 \\\\ z-2w &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-w+2 \\\\ y &=5 \\\\ z &=2w+4 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-w+2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2w+4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54dd2578-d394-54ec-aec7-cabb75370975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w-2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -3w-2 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716860} {:answer/id #uuid "61a6b605-b683-5828-96fa-57b6c73a4b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+1 \\\\ -w+2 \\\\ -3w+4 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716864} {:answer/id #uuid "989acd32-39a8-5e4e-9590-619fec9f9696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w-2 \\\\ -w+2 \\\\ -3w-5 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716872} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b0b583-8ea4-5482-adac-428d3641bef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+6 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -3w-1 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716875} {:answer/id #uuid "a858c37b-86e0-5f4f-a842-0dd87315492a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w+6 \\\\ -w+3 \\\\ -3w+3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716860} :answer-field/id #uuid "9efdfec5-c2c7-5319-a233-c6a0e0d410b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "74dce9a3-768f-5c83-8523-2ecf59814a1b" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y-4z-8w &=-6 \\\\ x+4y+z+8w &=-24 \\\\ -x+5z+14w &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -4 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1 & 8 & -24 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 & 14 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & 2 & -4 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1 & 8 & -24 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 & 14 & -8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1 & 8 & -24 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 & 14 & -8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 12 & -21 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 & 14 & -8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 12 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 10 & -11\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 10 & -11\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 6 & -4\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & -2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+w &=-2 \\\\ y+w &=-5 \\\\ z+3w &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-w-2 \\\\ y &=-w-5 \\\\ z &=-3w-2 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-w-2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -3w-2 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f26853b-1115-52d8-8583-316d07bec957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2z-6 \\\\ z+3 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716890} {:answer/id #uuid "97065a86-be3b-57e2-a7e0-92ed02cd96c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2z-4 \\\\ z+5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716901} {:answer/id #uuid "a142e1f6-289f-58b8-87ae-c920f0b560c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2z-4 \\\\ z+2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716902} {:answer/id #uuid "dec0d7e9-0463-540f-b6fc-f4ba97209710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2z-5 \\\\ z+3 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716907} {:answer/id #uuid "eabfc8dc-3d3f-5a6e-b4d8-5e308ffdaad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2z-6 \\\\ z+5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716901} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f262d9b-ffa7-52a7-8dd8-7f1da64339d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "16ce3401-e3ba-5cdc-835c-3c76ec99f364" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+8z &=-28 \\\\ -x+5y-7z &=29 \\\\ x-3y+5z &=-19.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 8 & -28 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -7 & 29 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 & -19\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 8 & -28 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -7 & 29 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 & -19\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -14 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -7 & 29 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 & -19\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 & -19\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 & -19\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2z &=-4 \\\\ y-z &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and we have one free variable, $z$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2z-4 \\\\ y &=z+5 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2z-4 \\\\ z+5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d376ba7-d959-51df-b0cf-e88b0e1e2181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3z+3 \\\\ -2z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716888} {:answer/id #uuid "5c294a08-d887-5166-9ae3-021c19ea289f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3z-2 \\\\ -2z+2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716893} {:answer/id #uuid "96fb3766-2444-5f68-8f38-adb6fea152cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3z+3 \\\\ -2z-3 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716900} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e249de-c3a6-5173-ae8b-b6e080cec5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3z-2 \\\\ -2z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716905} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fb340b-9aa5-57a7-9110-d550c085f109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3z+2 \\\\ -2z+2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716910}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716888} :answer-field/id #uuid "79cb1bed-6e11-5e9b-9331-3fb2c6e616f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "71106ed0-a837-5ba4-907a-dfda38b92b00" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y-10z &=8 \\\\ -x+4y+11z &=-7 \\\\ -2x+y+8z &=-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -2 & -10 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 11 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -2 & -10 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 11 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 11 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3z &=3 \\\\ y+2z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and we have one free variable, $z$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3z+3 \\\\ y &=-2z-1 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3z+3 \\\\ -2z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43a299f0-a0cb-51f4-a428-8d9ceb649d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -z+2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716891} {:answer/id #uuid "903dd306-39c9-5740-8019-7ba98675ac31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -z-3 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716899} {:answer/id #uuid "cf016e88-bcea-5093-9fc9-dc23b3ea31d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -z-6 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716906} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f0e283-7644-5c83-8e64-43638ba63503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -z-3 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716909} {:answer/id #uuid "fa77c56f-0bfa-5350-96bb-7c87fa6e5721" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -z+2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716912}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716899} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ecf2af-d63f-52b5-9303-72fdd10d1090" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7c43a147-b22c-5eb8-bcc9-0104e03fb636" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y+4z &=-18 \\\\ -x+y+z &=0 \\\\ 2x+2y+2z &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 4 & -18 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & -12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 4 & -18 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & -12\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & -12\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & -12\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & -12\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3 \\\\ y+z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and we have one free variable, $z$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3 \\\\ y &=-z-3 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -z-3 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1333fd86-4cc0-5a3d-9183-8c13558c1ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716886} {:answer/id #uuid "25e5322c-673d-59f5-bebc-7dd1c263a45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716889} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6e45b3-73fa-58ae-8ee0-6abb8b917afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z+6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716904} {:answer/id #uuid "e00f39d1-c513-572d-bc01-f54feb6647a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716908} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe00639-a4fa-5e69-9baa-22b5862b59ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716913}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716913} :answer-field/id #uuid "8124ec9c-3515-50f8-aa4e-f17978ba4e55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a3dc2d8d-76e5-56dc-9b40-78dc093d296d" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+8z &=-8 \\\\ 2x-y+8z &=-5 \\\\ 2x-3y+8z &=-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 8 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 8 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z &=-2 \\\\ y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and we have one free variable, $z$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-4z-2 \\\\ y &=1 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4z-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}]}
